'''Natravis DeVone Claybrooks''' (born September 15, 1977) is an American former professional [[gridiron football|football]] [[defensive tackle]] and coach. He played [[college football]] at [[East Carolina Pirates football|East Carolina]]. He was a defensive tackle in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) for seven teams ([[Green Bay Packers|Packers]], [[Tampa Bay Buccaneers|Buccaneers]], [[Cleveland Browns|Browns]], [[San Francisco 49ers|49ers]], [[Atlanta Falcons|Falcons]], [[Dallas Cowboys|Cowboys]], and [[Arizona Cardinals|Cardinals]]). Claybrooks was also a member of the [[Montreal Alouettes]] and [[Calgary Stampeders]] of the [[Canadian Football League]] (CFL). He was later the head coach of the CFL's [[BC Lions]].
